搭档组合，以及你们多年来所做的一切，我都在摄像机后面看着，

716
00:28:05.310 --> 00:28:08.510
and years, and it was such a gift for me.
这对我来说是一份巨大的礼物。

717
00:28:09.050 --> 00:28:14.370
There was not a day that went by that I didn't wake up in gratitude and say, what are we doing?
没有哪一天我不是怀着感激醒来，心想，我们在做什么呀？

718
00:28:15.190 --> 00:28:23.590
This is crazy fun and magic with this group of people who love the work so much and each
这群热爱工作也彼此热爱的人在一起，真是疯狂、有趣又神奇，

719
00:28:23.590 --> 00:28:27.070
other, you know, and it will never happen again.
你知道，这种事再也不会发生了。

720
00:28:27.250 --> 00:28:32.650
That kind of chemistry, that kind of energy will never, ever be replicated.
那种化学反应，那种能量，永远、永远无法被复制。

721
00:28:32.650 --> 00:28:39.590
And so seeing you guys during that audition process, it was hard, too, because there weren't
所以看到你们经历试镜过程时，其实也很艰难，因为当时电视上并没有

722
00:28:39.590 --> 00:28:42.210
any talking heads really yet on television.
真正意义上的访谈片段。

723
00:28:42.870 --> 00:28:47.390
And the rhythm was so much different, which is why we did, you know, produced auditions,
而且节奏完全不同，这就是为什么我们做了，你知道，制作过的试镜，

724
00:28:47.570 --> 00:28:49.230
where we did screen tests.
也就是我们做的试镜测试。

725
00:28:49.610 --> 00:28:53.330
Because if we would have gone into the network and you guys would have done a scene, they
因为如果我们直接去电视台，你们演了一场戏，他们

726
00:28:53.330 --> 00:28:55.250
would have said, you people are crazy.
肯定会说，你们这些人疯了吧。

727
00:28:55.250 --> 00:28:57.890
We will never make this show.
我们绝不会制作这部剧。

728
00:28:58.170 --> 00:29:01.930
So just the whole rhythms of it, the hard pauses.
所以整个节奏，那些刻意的停顿。

729
00:29:02.410 --> 00:29:08.990
That is something that I think is really amazing and such great, I mean, smart foresight on how
我认为这真的很了不起，而且非常有远见，知道该如何

730
00:29:08.990 --> 00:29:09.690
to sell the show.
推销这部剧。

731
00:29:09.810 --> 00:29:15.490
But a lot of times when you audition and you make it to that final stage where you go in
但很多时候，当你试镜并进入最后阶段，站在

732
00:29:15.490 --> 00:29:21.110
front of a room of 50 network execs, you kind of go into like a little theater, like a mini
50个电视台高管面前时，你就像走进了一个小剧场，一个小型的

733
00:29:21.110 --> 00:29:27.050
theater, and you do your scene as an actor in front of this room of people, and it's
剧场，作为演员在这一屋子人面前表演你的场景，这

734
00:29:27.050 --> 00:29:34.170
like doing a little mini scene at like a play, like a play, but for The Office, you guys filmed
就像在演一出小短剧，但对于《办公室》来说，你们把它

735
00:29:34.170 --> 00:29:39.170
it, produced it, and played it for the network so they could see what the show would look
拍摄、制作出来，并放给电视台看，这样他们就能看到这部剧看起来

736
00:29:39.170 --> 00:29:39.930
and feel like.
和感觉起来是什么样子的。

737
00:29:39.970 --> 00:29:41.650
And I just think that's so smart.
我真的觉得这太聪明了。

738
00:29:41.910 --> 00:29:47.430
I'm curious, after we shot the pilot and we were waiting to hear if we were going to
我很好奇，在我们拍完试播集等待消息，看我们是否会被

739
00:29:47.430 --> 00:29:51.790
get picked up, how close did we come to not getting picked up?
预订时，我们离被拒绝有多近？

740
00:29:51.930 --> 00:30:00.630
Because from my perspective, that phone call came like 24 hours before you announced it in
因为从我的角度来看，那个电话是在你们宣布消息前24小时

741
00:30:00.630 --> 00:30:01.070
New York.
才打到纽约的。

742
00:30:01.390 --> 00:30:02.530
That's exactly right.
完全正确。

743
00:30:02.810 --> 00:30:05.290
So they were deciding up until the last minute?
所以他们真的是在最后一刻才做决定？

744
00:30:05.530 --> 00:30:05.990
Yes.
是的。

745
00:30:06.170 --> 00:30:06.350
Wow.
哇。

746
00:30:06.430 --> 00:30:15.730
And we got the pickup contingent on being able to produce the episodes for under a million dollars.
而且我们获得预订的前提是，每集制作成本必须控制在一百万美元以下。

747
00:30:16.250 --> 00:30:17.570
And is that hard to do?
那很难做到吗？

748
00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:18.790
So was not...
所以并不是……

749
00:30:21.920 --> 00:30:22.680
Just like...
就像……

750
00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:24.280
I think a knife just came out of my eyeball.
我觉得我的眼球里刚才飞出了一把刀。

751
00:30:25.940 --> 00:30:28.680
Terri did like a whiplash look to Jenna, like...
泰瑞猛地转头看向珍娜，就像……

752
